# PARKED — Woodpecker only reads .yaml/.yml, so this file is inert.
#
# Enable it by renaming to `release.yaml`, but not before a macOS agent exists. With no agent
# carrying the `platform: darwin/amd64` label, a tag queues this pipeline against a runner that
# never appears: it hangs pending rather than failing, which is worse than not running at all.
#
# **Do not point this at the workstation.** Two reasons, in order of importance:
#
#   1. A release build pegs every core for about a minute. This project's premise is that the
#      audio render thread is the only clock and nothing may perturb it (AGENT.md); a build
#      firing mid-take could corrupt a measurement in a way that looks like the player's own
#      timing. An unattended agent decides for itself when that happens.
#   2. The `local` backend runs pipeline commands as the agent's user, so anyone who can push
#      a branch can execute code on that host — which would be the machine holding the SSH
#      signing key.
#
# Until then, releases are cut locally and deliberately: STANDARDS.md §9.4.1.
#
# Release pipeline — runs on a tag.
#
# **Needs a macOS agent running the `local` backend.** The app links AVFoundation, CoreMIDI
# and AppKit, and `build-app.sh` calls `codesign`, so this cannot run in a Linux container
# however the pipeline is written. The `local` backend runs the commands directly on the
# agent host rather than in an image, which is why no `image:` is given below.
#
# Agent setup, once, on a Mac that has Xcode 14.2:
#
#   WOODPECKER_BACKEND=local \
#   WOODPECKER_AGENT_SECRET=... \
#   WOODPECKER_SERVER=<host>:9000 \
#   WOODPECKER_FILTER_LABELS=platform=darwin/amd64 \
#   woodpecker-agent
#
# Tag and push to trigger:  git tag -s v0.2.0 -m 'v0.2.0' && git push origin v0.2.0

when:
  - event: tag
    ref: refs/tags/v*

labels:
  platform: darwin/amd64

steps:
  - name: package
    commands:
      - ./scripts/package-release.sh "${CI_COMMIT_TAG}"

  - name: publish
    # Uploads the artifacts to the Gitea release for this tag. Needs a Gitea API token with
    # write:repository, stored as the `gitea_token` secret in Woodpecker — never in the repo.
    image: woodpeckerci/plugin-gitea-release
    settings:
      base_url: https://git.heftyb.com
      files:
        - dist/*.zip
        - dist/*.sha256
        - dist/VERSION.txt
      api_key:
        from_secret: gitea_token
      title: "${CI_COMMIT_TAG}"
